  "id": "social-anxiety",
  "term": "social anxiety",
  "definition": "Social anxiety is a common anxiety disorder in which a person feels strong fear or anxiety in social situations where they might be watched, evaluated, or judged by other people. This can include public speaking, meeting new people, interviews, asking for help, or even everyday activities like eating, drinking, or using a public restroom in front of others because of fear of humiliation, rejection, or negative judgment.",
